===Etymology===
Old High German ''[[miluh]]'', akin to Old Saxon ''[[miluk]]''. Compare Danish ''[[mælk]]'', Dutch ''[[melk]]'', West Frisian ''[[molke]]'', Norwegian ''[[melk]]'', Old English ''[[meolc]]'', English ''[[milk]]'', Swedish ''[[mjölk]]'', Yiddish [[מילך]] (milkh).

===Noun===
'''Milch''' {{f}}

# [[milk|Milk]]
# [[white|White]] [[fluid]] that is [[exuded]] by certain [[plants]]
# A [[white]] [[liquid]] that is a [[mixture]] of other [[substances]], where one of the components is very finely distributed
# [[semen|Semen]] of male [[fish]]

